// @emit-error emitProgram: `?.` over a nullable struct has no `if` blocktype for this field's rep
// CONTRACT (must-error): the two field reps `p?.f ?? d` still cannot carry, kept LOUD rather
// than widened into check-clean invalid wasm. Its numeric siblings all lower now
// (`structs/optional-chain-wide-scalar-fields.vl`); these two were BUILT and MEASURED and
// then reverted, which is why they are filed rather than merely absent
// (`silent-class-inventory` D783).
//
//   STRING field — `fbIfRef(sTypeIdx)` spells the blocktype and the value arm is right, but
//   the DEFAULT (a string literal in a value position under this `if`) builds a module the
//   engine refuses, "Invalid input WebAssembly code": the literal's scratch reservation is
//   decided by a scan that has no arm for this site.
//
//   VALUE-UNION field — `fbIfRef(uBoxIdx)` spells the blocktype and `emitUnionCoerce` boxes
//   the default, both of which were written; the module is STILL invalid, and not at the
//   `if` — `const v = (x?.y) ?? 5` classifies its binding cell from a `??` whose left side is
//   an optional chain, and nothing on that path calls the value a box:
//   `type mismatch: expected i32, found (ref $type)`. A rep decision away, not a blocktype.
//
// The NARROWED spelling of both runs today (`if x != null { print(x.y) }`), which is what
// makes these capability gaps rather than rules.
type Bs = { y: string }
function fs(x: Bs | null) { print((x?.y) ?? "z") }
fs(null)
